 "reading": "Gain 4 applies (swing x3.926, clipped at =3,0U). The eye is as open as at gain 1 (0.998 both). Noise on A1 rises x3.20 against the x3.93 swing. Here the rise and fall times did NOT take run-level values: gain 1 held 57.3/58.4 ns and gain 4 held 66.3/68.8 ns over five rounds each (sd 0.05 and 0.0), so gain 4 is 9.0 and 10.4 ns slower. In quadrature that is a 33 and 35 ns extra time constant, an ADC-and-PGA bandwidth of the order of 10 MHz (rise ~ 0.35/BW), but the gain-1 figure is the 57 ns montreal5 also saw and run-level modes were seen there (88 ns), so this is one sample of the mode set, not a bandwidth measurement. n4 is about 1.1 codes at n1 = 0.70 and the model that gives it is inconsistent between gain 2 and gain 4.",
 "not_done": "No arm with probes, and no single-channel A1 (the board cannot); the same-board DAC0->A0 ETS path was not available on this wiring."
